From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 13:29:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] node-executor: add coordinated local executor pools

Allow root Node action modules to request bounded named local executor pools and preserve the required assignment through bundling, deployment, durable source metadata, archives, and execution routing. Validate the complete topology and steady-plus-surge RSS budget before commit and during startup.

Keep healthy default and named generations serving while one globally coordinated candidate starts, passes health checks, and prepares source and external packages without importing application code. Promote atomically, close old admission, and retain exact cleanup and surge ownership until the old direct child is reaped. Keep unhealthy, shutdown, and cgroup-pressure retirement immediate.

Reserve deployment cutover capacity before commit with exact recoverable claims, roll committed cutovers across affected pools, coalesce routine rotations, and support bounded explicit force reclamation without terminating the only serving generation before promotion. Carry signed package-readiness authority, expose bounded lifecycle and coordinator telemetry, and document the composed package, resilience, memory, and routing contracts.

Add focused coverage for declaration and metadata validation, package readiness, promotion and drain ownership, exceptional cleanup retries, deployment recovery, topology removal and reintroduction, pressure handling, global capacity serialization, startup budgets, and metric-label lifecycle.
